# Git remotes (Ensemble v2)

This repo has **two GitHub remotes**. When the user says **push to git** (or similar), push **only** to the **team org repo** — not the personal fork unless they explicitly ask.

## Remotes

| Remote | URL | Use |
|--------|-----|-----|
| **`ensemble`** | `https://github.com/Ensemble-Digital-Labs/ensmeblewebsite.git` | **Canonical team repo** — default push target |
| **`origin`** | `https://github.com/giachinh1/ensemblev2.git` | Personal fork — **do not push here** unless user explicitly asks |

## Default push behavior

When the user asks to push to GitHub / git (e.g. “push to git”, “update github”, “push hot git”):

1. Commit first if there are uncommitted changes (only when they asked to push/commit).
2. Push **`staging`** to **`ensemble`** only:

```bash
git push ensemble staging
```

3. Confirm on: `https://github.com/Ensemble-Digital-Labs/ensmeblewebsite/tree/staging`

If they name a different branch, push that branch to **`ensemble`** (not `origin`).

**Do not** push to both remotes unless the user explicitly asks for the fork too.

## Other branches

```bash
git push ensemble main
```

## Branch tracking

- Local `staging` may track `origin/staging` — ignore that for pushes; always use **`git push ensemble staging`**.
- Org repo name is spelled **`ensmeblewebsite`** (typo in remote URL — do not “fix”).

## Troubleshooting

If the user says they don’t see commits on GitHub, check whether the push went to `origin` instead of `ensemble`.
